topaz: 0951 - sweet USB at the khaje (SM6225) addresses

sweet's USB device/live-log stack (patches 0072-0077) was written for the
SM7150: GCC at 0x100000, DWC3 at 0xa600000, QUSB2 at 0x88e2000. Patch 0080
gates it behind sweethw=1 on topaz because with the SM7150 addresses it
pokes the wrong MMIO (and hangs).

The khaje (SM6225) blocks, from the phone's own kernel DT
(khaje-usb.dtsi / khaje.dtsi / bengal-gdsc.dtsi / gcc-bengal.c):

- GCC 0x1400000 (size 0x1f0000); USB30_PRIM GDSCR at +0x1a004
- DWC3 core 0x4e00000 (the ssusb@4e00000 wrapper block, 0x100000);
  the Qualcomm QSCRATCH wrapper is at its end: 0x4ef8800
- QUSB2 PHY 0x1613000
- clock branches (gcc-bengal.c): master 0x1a010, sleep 0x1a014,
  utmi 0x1a018, cfg_noc_usb3_prim_axi 0x1a084, sys_noc_usb3_prim_axi
  0x1a080, ahb2phy_usb 0x1d008, usb3_prim_clkref 0x9f000

The DWC3 register layout, the polled event handling and the ECM gadget
code are SoC-independent, so only the base addresses change. USB starts
unconditionally on topaz now; the SM7150 key/touch drivers still need
sweethw=1.

v2: the first version was malformed ("corrupt patch at line 62": hunks
without @@ headers, and a fake index line count). Rewritten as three
clean hunks with context lines, so git-am applies them.
